.TH SDL_GetRenderTextureAddressMode 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetRenderTextureAddressMode \- Get the texture addressing mode used in
.BR SDL_RenderGeometry ().

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetRenderTextureAddressMode(SDL_Renderer *renderer, SDL_TextureAddressMode *u_mode, SDL_TextureAddressMode *v_mode);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the rendering context\[char46]
.TP
.I u_mode
a pointer filled in with the
.BR SDL_TextureAddressMode
to use for horizontal texture coordinates in
.BR SDL_RenderGeometry (),
may be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I v_mode
a pointer filled in with the
.BR SDL_TextureAddressMode
to use for vertical texture coordinates in
.BR SDL_RenderGeometry (),
may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetRenderTextureAddressMode (3)
